# Copy to .env for a deployed-style build. Read at BUILD time (Vite inlines
# VITE_* values), so on Railway set them in the FRONTEND service's
# Variables and redeploy after changing one.

# The backend's public URL, e.g. https://backend-production-xxxx.up.railway.app
# (no trailing slash). Also added to the Content-Security-Policy so the site
# may talk to it.
# Leave it unset for local development: `npm run dev` forwards /api and
# /socket.io to the backend on localhost:4000 (vite.config.js), which also
# lets a phone use one HTTPS tunnel for both (README, "Running on a Phone").
VITE_API_URL=
